# Title: Potentially Suspicious Execution Of Regasm/Regsvcs From Uncommon Location
# ID: cc368ed0-2411-45dc-a222-510ace303cb2
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-08-25
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.009
# Description: Detects potentially suspicious execution of the Regasm/Regsvcs utilities from a potentially suspicious location
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((CommandLine:*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\* OR CommandLine:*\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\* OR CommandLine:*\\PerfLogs\\* OR CommandLine:*\\Users\\Public\\* OR CommandLine:*\\Windows\\Temp\\*)) AND (((Image:*\\Regsvcs.exe OR Image:*\\Regasm.exe)) OR ((OriginalFileName:"RegSvcs.exe" OR OriginalFileName:"RegAsm.exe"))))
